# Coach speech (Indonesian): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach says "kamu" and "aku" (glossary/id.md);
# Indonesian has no grammatical gender, so no word agrees with the player.
# Forms from common.lang: a move number is an ordinal, "di langkah {n:ord}" = "di langkah ke-12"
# (spoken "kedua belas"); an accuracy is "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "... persen"), also where
# English writes a bare {acc}; counts use count.* ("{n:piece}" = "3 buah catur", "{m:time}" = "2 kali").
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   bare nouns ("pembukaan"): a subject, or after "dalam" ("dalam permainan akhir").
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement said right after "remis", no comma ("Remis karena pat.").
#   theme.*             a verb phrase, no full stop, said after a colon or after "berlatihlah",
#                       "biasakan", "coba".
#   appraisal.level.*   the level name exactly as assets/i18n/id.lang shows it (coach.level.<n>.name),
#                       always after the word "tingkat" (the UI's word for a level): "tingkat Pemula".
# {opening:def} inside a sentence, {opening} when the name stands alone or after a label.

# ---- Names used inside the lines ------------------------------------------------------------------
appraisal.phase.opening = pembukaan
appraisal.phase.middlegame = permainan tengah
appraisal.phase.endgame = permainan akhir
